{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1297345-ideas-for-new-take-on-mummy","id":1297345,"title":"Ideas for new take on Mummy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-16T13:38:55-07:00","id":1297345,"title":"Ideas for new take on Mummy","content":"Here's an idea I had about Mummies<br /> Mind that I own the first editions, only had a quick read of Resurrection years ago, and never read Mummy the Curse.<br /> I've read some stuff on the fan wikis today and imagined some stuff that seems workable for player characters in a V5 game (or at least with a similar feel)<br /> <br /> The idea is to make the mummies as undead monsters again, not immortal beings<br /> <br /> The premise is that the player characters are modern day mummies.<br /> Modern day in the sense that they were mortals up to recent times, and then they were taken and buried alive in terrible rituals (you know, like in the movie)<br /> After a certain amount of time, 5 to 20 years depending on the burial and mummification methods, the new mummy rise from the grave and become a Deathless (modern day mummy)<br /> <br /> Most often than not this process is made by an ancient mummy whose Rite (the Spell of Life) is failing to keeping her or him alive after millenia, and so the ancient mummy attempts to recruit a new soldier for Maat using his Sekhem and necromantic energies coupled with a bastardized version of the Spell of Life.<br /> Which naturally doesn't work well in the Final Nights, generating not an immortal but an undead monster.<br /> It also destroys the ancient mummy in the process, which may or may not leave some memories with the newly created Deathless.<br /> (yeah in a way many new mummies have a &quot;sire&quot;)<br /> Relatively new mummies can make an attempt to make new Deathless if aided by cultists and such, and they can actually succeed; but this &quot;second generation&quot; mummy will lack a few advantages. Newest cults can even attempt this without a mummy's powers and sometimes they can suceed too<br /> <br /> If you need an in-universe explanation, imagine a soft retcon where most of the mummies went Shuankhsen after the Sixth Maelstrom but they were still affected by it. And so they started to decay, whiter, etc. So to defend Balance they went on recruitment.<br /> While the mummies that accepted to become Amenti are very few, and most are bent on the destruction of old-style mummies (and of the player characters)<br /> Buuuuut most of this stuff should really stay unexplained, at least in-game. It really cancels out mystery and mysticism otherwise<br /> <br /> So the modern day mummies awake from the dead in their &quot;tumuli&quot;, their special tombs, and the whole idea is that they know very little about the whys and hows (compare them with thin blood vampires). They can take information from texts and hyeroglyphs in their tumulus, and from cultists if they meet one.<br /> They also have a &quot;death sight&quot; which makes them identify undead at first glance.<br /> Probably they can perceive other mummies at distance. This way even if a big city will have just a handful of mummies they will know each other.<br /> <br /> Also modern mummies suffer from the same problem of the ancient ones, they whiter and become progressively mummy-like.<br /> They can reverse the process absorbing enough life force, but of course fueling &quot;disciplines&quot; with life force will instead accelerate the process.<br /> Absorbing life force should be an appropriately nasty affair<br /> <br /> I'd say they also need to sleep in their &quot;sarcophagus&quot; to heal aggravated damage, and take some advantage by bangages and such<br /> This way it should give the feeling of playing a more classic monster-like mummy<br /> <br /> Also, suicide doesn't work. You are deathless<br /> Many modern mummies go insane eventually, succumb to corruption and become &quot;wyrm-mummies&quot;<br /> <br /> So a mummy character will usually have to:<br /> 1) figure out the whys and whats<br /> 2) deal with a world that thought you dead for a decade<br /> 3) not whiter<br /> 4) fight the forces of unbalance (well, more like the forces of unbalance will come for you and you will have to fend them off)<br /> <br /> I'd allow mummies from various cultures and parts of the world, not just three. I'd take the idea from Mummy the Curse that all mummies originated from a common history at the dawn of time. But I'd avoid to invent a mythology. The Vampire route, twisting an existing myth (Caine) and making it the hypothetical foundation that you can take as metaphor or truth is a much better route (personal opinion of course).<br /> The Great Serpent (Apep, the Wyrm, etc.), Osiris, Isis, Set are figures with parallels in most mythologies. The egyptian mummies insist their is the &quot;true&quot; version of the story of course, much as Followers of Set did, and much like with Caine other cultures will say that's not true.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this are just general ideas that popped out of my head today.<br /> I'm curious about others' opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T17:17:38-07:00","id":1299783,"title":"","content":"You put a lot of thought into this, and I respect that. I can't say that I'm a fan. I really love what they did with Resurrection, keeping it in the World of Darkness but also providing a splat that wasn't something inherently cursed or doomed to fail and wasn't another type of dead thing wandering around and lamenting over their condition. I also loved hope, redemption, second chances, and responsibility as themes. I might take a look at something similar to this as a new kind of enemy, something stronger than an Asekh-sen, but weaker than the Apepnu, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T07:09:55-07:00","id":1299939,"title":"","content":"Hey thanks for the response <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, my idea was to have mummy characters who were actually playable in a Vampire chronicle. So, as you well said, the idea of cursed and doomed were fundamental to the idea.<br /> And for the &quot;dead thing wandering and lamenting&quot;... I think it ties well with the classic monster type.<br /> Don't get me wrong, I love Mage and especially Werewolf. And Werewolf really distance itself from the classic monster werewolves. I love them. But also makes them unplayable in your average vampire chronicle (my personal opinion of course)<br /> <br /> As you say, the whole Resurrection thing felt very distant from the typical horror themes. From what little I know of it, it feels &quot;truly immortal divine-powered beings&quot;<br /> <br /> Also I think in 2nd edition they were too much focused in:<br /> A) tying with historical mythology facts<br /> B) crossovering with other game lines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T20:58:11-07:00","id":1301012,"title":"","content":"Ravnos, with the Amenti, they can work well in a game with the other splats, but it depends entirely upon the concept behind the Amenti in question. I'm not arguing against what you said when I say this, but when someone feels like they can't really mesh, I often find that it's because they aren't so familiar with the complexities of the game (mummy). Now, that doesn't mean that I feel that they should be in every vampire game or every werewolf game, etc. I just mean that they can work and work well. For example, if your party has characters that genuinely wish to uphold their humanity and one or more characters trying to atone (trying for Golconda isn't necessary but would obviously fall under this), or even if the characters are simply in that Humanity 6+ range and share a common enemy. I could honestly list a whole bunch of things, but I'd just leave it there. I think that what you have in mind sounds really good for your game, and like I said before, while I wouldn't use it for PC mummies, it gave Me ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:22:03-07:00","id":1301278,"title":"","content":"Ah well, my personal opinion is that very few splats mesh well with each other, especially OWoD. Some are philosophically too divergent with their themes and others are too limited in action (plainly vampires can act freely only in nighttime). But of course is just my personal opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I feel that with some reworking the mummy classic concept (which diverges from the official game line) and wraiths too could work as alternatives for undead characters in a V5 game. But it would still be mainly a V5 game. At least that were my thoughts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And glad my thoughts bear some fruits for you. I can see that my ideas could give some different ones in more classical games, like an overpopulation of &quot;corrupted or incomplete new breed of mummies&quot; that must dealt with (either with brutal force or a correct application of the Spell of Life if possible)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}